  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Thursday)\nIssued at 1235 AM CDT Fri Oct 9 2026\n\nUpper level ridging will develop across the Plains this weekend into \nnext week, as an upper level trough materializes off the coast of \nCalifornia and into the Desert Southwest. This pattern will result \nin dry conditions through Tuesday, with above normal temperatures \ninto the middle of next week. The warmest temperatures are expected \nMonday through Wednesday, when forecasted highs climb into the low \nto mid 90s for much of the area. \n\nSouthwest flow aloft develops across the area by the middle of next \nweek, in advance of the upper trough over the southern Rockies by \nthis time. Models show this system lifting northeast across the \nCentral Plains by late week, with a trailing portion of the trough \nextending southwest across the southern Rockies and Desert \nSouthwest. An increase in moisture, coupled with several \ndisturbances passing through will support scattered showers and \nstorms beginning Wednesday and persisting through Friday. In \naddition, models show a cold front affecting the area by Friday, \nwhich will bring an end to the above normal temperatures.",
